Original commit body from d0b0a206aff7069b0b44e9323de12aff6c839cac:

Symbols minted outside a language analyzer with a language were reached by
neither the backstop floor (it runs before the linkers) nor the Class-B
chokepoint (language=None only): the gRPC linker's services, servicers and
stubs and the view-template linker's templates shipped stable_id=null, and
manifest_targets' build targets (Package.swift, Gradle, Cabal ...) rode the
floor key. One shared helper now mints them: overload_arity.scoped_stable_id
(declared_arity_stable_id over a scope chain held as a list) and its wrapper
pass_minted_stable_id, whose chain is led by the minting pass. A static scan
in the floor gate fails any future language-bearing Symbol(...) minted
outside an analyzer without a stable_id.

The gate (test_stable_id_floor_gate.py) now counts EVERY kind (it counted
callables and members), runs the pipeline with include_docs so doc/config
kinds are seen, matches deletion survivors by (kind, name, line, col), and
gains 34 fixtures (css, dockerfile, hcl, latex, just, makefile, mermaid,
toml, xml, json, ansible, blade, handlebars, graphql, vhdl, verilog, smithy,
kdl, sparql, robot, puppet, bitbake, prisma, ini, properties, markdown, rst,
svelte, vue, astro, meson, requirements, gitignore, bibtex) plus extra files
reaching the linker/pass mints (gRPC servicer, Django view + template,
Package.swift, build.gradle, .cabal). Folded into floor_and_null rather than
a new section: that section was already empty, and one census over all kinds
needs no second definition.

Every non-callable kind still on floor/null migrated floor->producer with
its grammar's scope chain: dockerfile (stage), make (conditional branch),
cmake (enclosing block), css (at-rules + rule selector), toml/json manifest
entries, ansible (play), android xml (full name), bash alias (functions),
latex (sections), just (attributes as decorators, parameters to
meta.parameters), handlebars (open blocks), graphql non-table kinds, hcl
(provider alias), vhdl (entity/architecture), mermaid (diagram), blade,
gnuplot plot (plotted text), erlang record, r source (function chain).
Table kinds keep their table formulas (base.is_table_kind). Julia now emits
`function Base.show(...)`, `Base.length(x) = ...` and zero-method
`function f end` (decorator "generic").

Floor/null -> producer only: every previously produced id is byte-identical
(24,079 + 4,761 ids on two corpus samples, 1,064 on the gate fixtures; the
only fixture ids that differ are solidity's, which vary with the checkout
path on dev as well). Corpus floor/null all kinds: 333 -> 0 (code sample),
1,083 -> 0 (config sample). Gate: floor_and_null stays empty over every kind;
sibling_deletion_moves 15 -> 29 languages, the 14 added being what the wider
measurement finds (doc family hashing line numbers via make_doc_stable_id,
and bibtex whose stable_id is its node id): value-changing, scheme batch.

